    "result_text": "All good \u2014 AcceptanceTest is the only test class (the others are support classes) and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the direct level rules with a points system.\n\n**New file** `MembershipPoints.java` \u2014 a small self-contained helper (matching the codebase's existing `AgeBand`/`CheckDigit` static-helper idiom) with two tiny methods:\n- `of(owner)` \u2192 points: +2 email, +1 namesakeCount 0, +2 household of 3+, +3 tenure over 365 days.\n- `level(points)` \u2192 1 (0-1), 2 (2-3), 3 (4-5), 4 (6+).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping and reduced the existing `membershipLevel` default method to a two-line delegation into the helper. Both fields are now returned.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field and widened `membershipLevel` to 1\u20134 with the new description, so the generated DTO carries both fields.\n\nStructural impact was kept low by putting all the new branching in a fresh low-complexity class rather than growing `OwnerMapper`: the only method I edited there is now trivial (CC ~1), and I added just one mapping annotation line.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsPointsAndLevel` (email + no namesake \u2192 3 points \u2192 level 2) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
