    "probe_text": "I have the full picture. Here is every validation and side-effect applied by `POST /api/owners`, in pipeline order (from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class).\n\n## Endpoint guard (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; unauthenticated/unauthorized requests are rejected before the pipeline runs.\n\n## The pipeline\n\n**1. `RequireDailyLimit`**\n- *Validation:* counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today (today rolled to the next business day). If \u2265 **100**, throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n**2. `RequireOwnerFields`** (the sole `@RequestBody` binding)\n- *Side-effect:* normalizes `address` in place (trim + collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n- *Validation:* requires non-null/non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`; any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n- *Side-effect:* republishes the body as an `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` variable for later steps.\n\n**3. `RequireValidPostcode`**\n- *Validation:* only if `postcode` present \u2014 must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) it must fall in range; otherwise `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**. Absent postcode is accepted.\n\n**4. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`**\n- *Side-effect:* rewrites `telephone` to E.164 in place \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+`, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`.\n- *Validation:* the digits after `+` must be 8-15 long, else `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"telephone\")` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**5. `ValidateTelephoneCountryLength`**\n- *Validation:* `+61` requires 9 national digits, `+1` requires 10; wrong length \u2192 **400**.\n\n**6. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`**\n- *Validation/side-effect:* only if `email` present \u2014 must match the email regex (else 400); then lower-cased in place; rejected if its domain is disposable (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400**. Absent email is untouched.\n\n**7. `RequireUniqueIdentity`** *(transaction begins here)*\n- *Validation:* builds `identityKey` = `telephone|email|\"\"` and rejects if it exactly matches an existing owner's \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n**8. `RequireUniqueHousehold`** *(transaction)*\n- *Validation:* skipped if `sharesHousehold` is true or postcode is blank/absent; otherwise rejects if `householdId` (last name + postcode) matches an existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n**9. `RequireCityCapacity`** *(transaction)*\n- *Validation:* rejects if the city (case-insensitive) already has \u2265 **50** owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n**10. `BuildOwner`** *(transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper.toOwner`.\n- *Validation:* if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is in the future \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**.\n- *Side-effect:* defaults `registrationDate` to today when absent, then rolls it forward off weekends to the next Monday; publishes `Out<Owner>`.\n\n**11. `AssignCustomerCode`** *(transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`).\n\n**12. `CountNamesakes`** *(transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**13. `CountHousehold`** *(transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `householdCount` = existing members with the same `householdId` **+ 1** (includes this new owner).\n\n**14. `FlagPossibleDuplicate`** *(transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* if `sharesHousehold` is true, sets `possibleDuplicate = false`; otherwise, if some existing owner shares last name + postcode (normalized) but has a different telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = that owner's id`; else `false`.\n\n**15. `SaveOwner`** *(transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* persists the owner via the repository (assigns its `id`).\n\n**16. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(transaction \u2014 commits at pipeline end)*\n- *Side-effect (derived DTO fields via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`):* `displayName`, `initials`, `telephoneDisplay`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `checkDigit` (Luhn over customerCode), `membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`.\n- *Side-effect:* computes `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > **80** owners were created today.\n- *Side-effect:* writes an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n- *Response:* **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n## Notes\n- Ordering is deliberate: field/format validation (steps 2-6) runs **before** the DB uniqueness/capacity checks (7-9), and normalization (address, telephone, email) happens before those checks so comparisons use canonical values.\n- Governance `transaction` spans steps 7-16, so all the reads and the save commit as a single transaction at the end.\n- Unmatched escalations fall through to the generic handlers in `officefloor/escalation/` (e.g. `java.lang.Exception.yml`, `NotFoundException.yml`).\n\nI didn't change anything \u2014 this is read-only analysis."
